From 83eeb4ff72cc7731de6b7f53d2cd522fecf74fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:11:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Syscalls: keep argv[0] for an FD execveat through the FEX
 loader

An execveat(fd, "", argv, envp, AT_EMPTY_PATH) that binfmt_misc can't take
(no FEX registration, or an FD_CLOEXEC fd that has to be copied) is
handed to the next FEX through FEX_EXECVEFD. That FEX loads from the FD
and uses the binfmt preserve-argv0 layout (FEX <path> <argv0> <argv1>...),
but the execve handler only kept the caller's argv[0] for the path-backed
loader FD, so the program saw its argv shifted by one: glibc's fexecve()
under FEX passed {"a", "b"} for {"argv0", "a", "b"}.

Keep argv[0] for every FD-backed load. A direct execveat (binfmt_misc
registered, FD without FD_CLOEXEC) is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
index 207c33b..e27c598 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp
@@ -447,9 +447,10 @@ uint64_t ExecveHandler(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame* Frame, const char* pathname
 
     // It is valid to provide nullptr first argument.
     if (*OldArgv) {
-      // The direct fallback uses the executable path as argv[0]. An FD-backed load uses the
-      // binfmt preserve-argv0 layout, so the caller-supplied argv[0] has to stay in the vector.
-      if (!NeedsLoaderFD) {
+      // The direct fallback uses the executable path as argv[0]. An FD-backed load (an FD execveat or
+      // the path-backed loader FD) uses the binfmt preserve-argv0 layout, so the caller-supplied
+      // argv[0] has to stay in the vector.
+      if (!IsFDExec && !NeedsLoaderFD) {
         ++OldArgv;
       }
       while (*OldArgv) {
